course: dictionary
lesson: 9422
title: Squirm and the feelings behind it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can describe a body or a feeling. To squirm means to twist and wriggle, like a child on a hard carpet. «The squirming, star-fish-shaped baby» in the story is wriggling and twisting, trying to get free.
explain: Squirm can also describe a feeling inside you. When something embarrasses you, your body may twist about as if you want to hide. The word cringe is slang for that feeling. «Some embarrassing moments make you cringe for weeks, and your whole body squirms as if it were happening again.»
explain: Use the words around squirm to find its meaning. A puppy that wriggles out of your arms is trying to get free. A child asked a hard question in class may squirm because they feel uncomfortable. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: You may also meet the phrases squirm in your seat and make someone squirm. To squirm in your seat means to keep wriggling because you are bored or uncomfortable. To make someone squirm means to make them feel embarrassed or uneasy.
fact: To squirm means to twist and wriggle your body, usually because you are uncomfortable, bored or trying to get free.
fact: To squirm can also mean to feel very embarrassed or ashamed.
fact: Squirm can be a verb or a noun: a squirm is one wriggly movement.
fact: «Mortified» means extremely embarrassed, and «cringe» is slang for that squirming feeling.
fact: «Squirm out of» means to wriggle free of something.
exercise: «The squirming, star-fish-shaped baby» was carried outside. What is squirming here? | *Wriggling and twisting, trying to get free | Swimming in the sea | Sleeping peacefully in a cot | Singing a happy song
exercise: Mia's friend read her diary aloud, and Mia began to squirm. What does squirm show here? | Mia is very happy | *Mia feels embarrassed | Mia is trying to get out of a hug | Mia is cold
exercise: Which word is slang for the squirming feeling of embarrassment? | *cringe | carpet | castle | cheer
test:
Ben squirmed in his seat during the long maths lesson. What does squirmed mean here? | Sat very still and calm | *Twisted and wriggled because he was bored | Jumped up to sing | Fell asleep
«His joke about my spelling made me squirm.» What does squirm mean in this sentence? | Laughed loudly | Ran out of the room | *Felt embarrassed | Went very cold
exam: Which sentence uses squirm to mean feeling embarrassed? | The fish squirmed in the net and then swam free. | *Her question made me squirm in front of the whole class. | The puppy squirmed out of my arms.
